FINDINGS:
- [MAJOR] `src/runtime.rs:1680` — the numeric `time.format` branch now calls `formatted_date(tm.naive_utc(), …)`, and `formatted_date` (`src/runtime.rs:925`) takes a `NaiveDateTime`. A naive value has no zone, so valid layouts that render the UTC zone (`%Z`, `%z`, `%:z`, `%+`) now produce empty or offset-less output for a timestamp. `phases/phase-097/REPORT.md:26` says the numeric form returns exactly what it did before. Keep the UTC `DateTime` for the number branch (or make the formatter carry an optional zone) and add `time.format(0, "%Z")`/`"%z"` regression tests. What would settle it: run those two calls on the parent and on this tree; the old expected values are `UTC`/`+0000`.

- [MINOR] `SURVEY.md:102` — the `time` inventory row lists 13 members and omits `parse` and `from_unix`, while `src/stdlib.rs:128-145` has 15. The phase report claims an inventory of 63 dotted members, but this row enumerates only 61. `tests/stdlib_gap_survey_test.rs` reconciles module names and the builtin count, not member lists, so the gate does not catch it. Add both names to the row.

- [MINOR] `SURVEY.md:267` — the new rank-6 citation `src/runtime.rs:705` is a doc-comment line; `parse_iso8601` starts at `src/runtime.rs:715`. `SURVEY.md:269` cites `src/runtime.rs:1634` for formatting, but 1634 is the `time_now` arm; the formatter is at 1657 and its date branch at 1682-1683. `SURVEY.md:277` repeats the 705 citation. The citation test only checks that the line exists, so these are green but wrong.

- [MINOR] `src/runtime.rs:669` — `date_year` rejects fewer than four digits after the optional sign. The removed `time.unix` path parsed with chrono `%Y`, which accepts 1-3 digit years, so `time.unix("999-01-01 00:00:00")` (and `99-…`) previously produced seconds and now errors. This contradicts `phases/phase-097/REPORT.md:82` (“a superset … old callers keep their answers”). Either accept short years or record the narrowing as deliberate and test it. What would settle it: run the call on the parent and on this tree.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
